WEBVTT

00:00:03.447 --> 00:00:06.155
-Professor.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:20.711
Igor Karkaroff, you have been brought
from Azkaban at your own request...

00:00:20.962 --> 00:00:22.839
...to present evidence to this council.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.716
Should your testimony
prove consequential...

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:29.971
...council may be prepared
to order your immediate release.

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:34.725
Until such time, you remain in the eyes
of the Ministry a convicted Death Eater.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.477
Do you accept these terms?

00:00:37.228 --> 00:00:39.814
-I do, sir.
-And what do you wish to present?

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.608
I have names, sir.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:46.821
There was Rosier, Evan Rosier.

00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:51.993
-Rosier is dead.
-He took a piece of me with him...

00:00:52.243 --> 00:00:54.287
-...though, didn't he?
KARKAROFF: I didn't know.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.206
CROUCH: If that is all the witness has--
KARKAROFF: No, no, no.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.501
There was Rookwood! He was a spy.

00:01:00.751 --> 00:01:03.212
Augustus Rookwood?
Of the Department of Mysteries?

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.380
KARKAROFF:
Yeah, the same.

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:08.301
He passed information to You-Know-Who
from inside the Ministry itself.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:12.847
Very well. Council will deliberate.

00:01:13.014 --> 00:01:15.016
In the meantime,
you will return to Azkaban.

00:01:15.224 --> 00:01:19.854
No! Wait, please! Please, I have more!
What about Snape? Severus Snape?

00:01:20.021 --> 00:01:23.024
As the council is aware,
I've given evidence on this matter.

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:27.236
Severus Snape was indeed a Death Eater
and, prior to Lord Voldemort's downfall...

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.738
-...turned spy for us at
great personal risk.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.323
KARKAROFF: It's a lie!

00:01:30.406 --> 00:01:33.993
-Today he's no more a Death Eater than I.
-Snape remains faithful to the Dark Lord!

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.329
Silence!

00:01:37.038 --> 00:01:40.333
Unless the witness possesses
any genuine name of consequence...

00:01:40.541 --> 00:01:42.668
...this session is now concluded.

00:01:42.877 --> 00:01:44.921
Oh, no, no, no.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.340
I've heard about one more.

00:01:47.423 --> 00:01:50.176
CROUCH: What's that?
-The name.

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.677
-Yes?
-I know for a fact...

00:01:51.886 --> 00:01:53.930
...this person took part
in the capture...

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.265
...and, by means
of the Cruciatus Curse...

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:59.936
...torture of the Auror Frank Longbottom
and his wife!

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.355
CROUCH: The name.
Give me the wretched name!

00:02:02.563 --> 00:02:04.065
KARKAROFF:
Barty Crouch...

00:02:04.315 --> 00:02:05.816
[GASPS]

00:02:07.818 --> 00:02:08.903
...Junior.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:15.576
[GRUNTS]

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.081
MAN:
Hold him down!

00:02:23.668 --> 00:02:27.380
Get your filthy hands off me,
you pathetic little men!

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.591
Hello, Father.

00:02:32.093 --> 00:02:34.095
You are no son of mine.

00:02:36.097 --> 00:02:37.807
[YELLS]

00:02:42.937 --> 00:02:44.605
[PANTING]

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:49.860
Curiosity is not a sin, Harry.
But you should exercise caution.

00:02:51.362 --> 00:02:52.613
It's a Pensieve.

00:02:52.822 --> 00:02:57.410
Very useful if, like me,
you find your mind a wee bit stretched.

00:02:57.618 --> 00:03:01.247
It allows me to see once more
things I've already seen.

00:03:01.622 --> 00:03:04.500
You see, Harry, I have searched
and searched for something...

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.419
...some small detail...

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.880
...something I might have overlooked...

00:03:10.131 --> 00:03:14.385
...something that would explain why
these terrible things have happened.

00:03:15.136 --> 00:03:18.973
Every time I get close to an answer,
it slips away.

00:03:20.016 --> 00:03:21.517
It's maddening.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.646
Sir? Mr. Crouch's son.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.482
What exactly happened to him?

00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:33.446
He was sent to Azkaban.
Destroyed Barty to do it.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.783
But he had no choice.
The evidence was overwhelming.

00:03:39.368 --> 00:03:42.288
-Why do you ask?
-It's just that I....

00:03:42.997 --> 00:03:45.166
I had a dream about him.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.171
It was in the summer, before school.

00:03:52.423 --> 00:03:55.384
In the dream, I was in a house.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:04:00.389
And Voldemort was there,
only he wasn't quite human.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:04.143
And Wormtail was there too.
And Mr. Crouch's son.

00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:06.395
DUMBLEDORE:
Have there been others like this dream?

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:09.690
Yes. Always the same one.

00:04:12.777 --> 00:04:15.196
Sir, these dreams...

00:04:15.404 --> 00:04:20.493
...what I see, you don't think
it's actually happening, do you?

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.164
I think it's unwise for you
to linger over these dreams, Harry.

00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:27.500
I think it's best if you simply...

00:04:33.214 --> 00:04:34.965
...cast them away.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.601
KARKAROFF:
It's a sign, Severus.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:46.852
[DOOR OPENING]

00:04:47.061 --> 00:04:48.521
You know what it means as well as I.

00:04:56.946 --> 00:04:58.197
Potter!

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.825
What's your hurry?

00:05:05.955 --> 00:05:09.625
Congratulations, your performance
in the Black Lake was inspiring.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.211
Gillyweed, am I correct?

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.547
Yes, sir.

00:05:15.506 --> 00:05:16.757
Ingenious.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:22.555
A rather rare herb, gillyweed.

00:05:23.514 --> 00:05:26.892
Not something found
in your everyday garden.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.563
Nor is this.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:36.527
Know what it is?

00:05:37.653 --> 00:05:39.155
Bubble juice, sir?

00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:41.574
Veritaserum.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:46.036
Three drops of this and You-Know-Who
himself would spill his darkest secrets.

00:05:46.287 --> 00:05:51.500
The use of it on a student is,
regrettably, forbidden. However...

00:05:52.042 --> 00:05:55.129
...should you ever steal
from my personal stores again...

00:05:55.296 --> 00:06:00.134
...my hand might just slip over
your morning pumpkin juice.

00:06:00.301 --> 00:06:04.638
-I haven't stolen anything.
-Don't lie to me.

00:06:05.806 --> 00:06:11.604
Gillyweed may be innocuous,
but boomslang skin, lacewing flies?

00:06:12.313 --> 00:06:15.608
You and your little friends are brewing
Polyjuice Potion, and believe me...

00:06:15.691 --> 00:06:17.943
...I'm going to find out why!

00:06:19.570 --> 00:06:20.654
[CHEERING]

00:06:20.821 --> 00:06:22.698
[MARCHING BAND PLAYING]

00:06:39.548 --> 00:06:41.634
[CHANTING IN FRENCH]

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.472
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

